THIRD-PARTY DATA — PROVENANCE AND TERMS
================================================================================

Spectroscopic and atmospheric reference data are obtained from external
databases. Each carries its provider's own usage and citation obligations,
which the end user is responsible for meeting when running the package.

1. HITRAN line lists and Collision-Induced Absorption (CIA)
   Provider : HITRAN database, hitran.org
   Files    : *.par line lists; data/cia/*.cia
   Terms    : HITRAN data are provided for the user's own use under HITRAN's
              data-use policy and do NOT carry a redistribution license. Users
              must obtain these files themselves from hitran.org and cite the
              current HITRAN edition. This package does not grant any right to
              redistribute HITRAN data.
   Cite     : Gordon et al., JQSRT 277, 107949 (2022) — HITRAN2020.
              Karman et al., Icarus 328, 160–175 (2019) — CIA.
   See      : data/cia/SOURCE.md

2. TIPS-2024 total internal partition sums
   Provider : R. R. Gamache et al. (HITRAN partition functions)
   Cite     : Gamache et al., JQSRT 345, 109509 (2025).

3. MT-CKD continuum (H2O and CO2 coefficient tables)
   Provider : Atmospheric and Environmental Research (AER), AER-RC/MT_CKD
   Files    : data/mt_ckd_h2o/mt_ckd43_h2o_coeffs.csv;
              data/mt_ckd_co2/mt_ckd_co2_coeffs.csv
   Terms    : AER MT_CKD is open-source and redistributable with attribution
              and its copyright notice retained.
   Cite     : Mlawer et al., Phil. Trans. R. Soc. A 370, 2520–2556 (2012).

4. AFGL standard atmospheres
   Provider : Air Force Geophysics Laboratory reference atmospheres
   Files    : data/afgl_*_50lev.csv
   Terms    : Public reference profiles, freely redistributable.
   Cite     : Anderson et al., AFGL-TR-86-0110 (1986).

5. CO2 line-mixing relaxation data
   Provider : Lamouroux / Hartmann et al. (HITRAN2020 line-mixing package)
   Cite     : Lamouroux et al., JQSRT 151, 88–96 (2015);
              Hartmann et al., JQSRT 110, 2019–2026 (2009).

